229 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 121 0 R/E(Sequoia Marine Solutions is a first-year company that has a C-Suite Executive team that works closely with the seven subsystem team leads, who in turn work with our general employees. SMS\220 seven subsystems are staffed with appropriate combinations of Mechanical Engineers and Computer/Electrical Engineers.)/Pg 11 0 R/K[24]>>
endobj

230 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 121 0 R/E(An important factor to every company is the official structure. Due to the team size and the newly established nature of the host club, SMS decided to establish a C-Suite, while having individual leads for different subsystems. This allows clearer communication, and a fuller picture for each employee. The rigid structure \(see Fig. 2\) was established early on, and influenced design processes as well as purchasing and other administrative duties.)/Pg 11 0 R/K[25]>>
endobj

231 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 121 0 R/E(As a new company, SMS is still working to develop a year-round schedule. To the right is our projected schedule, with December to May being accurate to this year\220s timeline. The goal is to onboard and train new members throughout the competition process. The Fall semester is spent learning from past experiences to identify overarching company goals. Winter break is focused around research, brainstorming, and developing of the company\220s planned solutions for given MATE tasks. Then, the Spring semester is the time for manufacturing, testing, and finalization.)/Pg 11 0 R/K[26]>>
endobj

