369 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 131 0 R/E(To complete the mission tasks, ROSIE uses a primary 2 DOF manipulator and secondary static end effectors.)/Pg 21 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

370 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 131 0 R/E(Claw Design: Uses a four-bar linkage system with the links in such a way that the opening/closing of the claw is powered by linear motion and achieves parallel motion when nearing full closure. To achieve this motion a leadscrew is mounted to a brushless motor. As the leadscrew rotates inside a heat set insert, the connector piece moves back and forwards moving the links in a way that opens and closes them.)/Pg 21 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

371 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 131 0 R/E(Rotation Design: The rotation ability of the manipulator is useful as it allows greater ability to pick up and manipulate objects, some tasks become impossible without this ability such as removing the biofouling. Uses a 2-gear drive. The driven gear is mounted concentrically with the leadscrew and is mounted to the back of the baseplate of the claw. The housing of the driven gear shaft also includes two pressfit bushings. The rotation gear is powered by a DD 3130 waterproof brushless motor and placed at the output of the two 1:4 gearboxes. These gearboxes help reduce the speed of rotation while increasing torque to the rotation gear giving precise control to the pilots to complete tasks more effectively and eliminates the need to make complex maneuvers that can damage props. The bushings and gearboxes are mounted to the t-slot rail in two stacked housing parts placed in front of the motors. The driven gear shaft slides into the bushings and a cap is attached with wire to the end of the shaft, thus mounting the gear and claw to the housing while still allowing it to rotate. Since both motors are rigidly mounted to the t-slot behind the rotation mechanism, the claw can be rotated indefinitely without worry of any motor wires binding up.)/Pg 21 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

372 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 131 0 R/E(Harpoon: Rigid manipulator that contains no moving parts. This manipulator is shaped like a harpoon with smooth fins inspired by the barbs of a harpoon. It was specifically designed for the task of picking up the basket stars. Due to its harpoon shape it can easily spear a basket star and use its barbs to hook it. Although it was made to pick up basket stars, testing has found that it can also easily hook the rope handles of the eDNA sensor. The harpoons are strong enough so that we can use 2 of them to pick up the lobster pot if needed.)/Pg 21 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

373 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 131 0 R/E(Manipulators)/Pg 21 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

374 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 131 0 R/E(Figure 20: Explode view of SMS\220s 2 DOF Manipulator)/Pg 21 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

