380 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 132 0 R/Pg 22 0 R/A[1388 0 R 0]/K[2]>>
endobj

381 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 132 0 R/E(3D Printed Gearbox: We used a free public design from a cad file sharing website and modified it to fit our purpose. The gearbox is a stackable planetary gearbox which offers a 1:4 ratio. The gearbox was resized to 70% its original size and input/output shafts were changed to better fit out needs. The input shaft was changed to mount directly to the rotation motor and the output shaft was made into a polygon. The polygon shape distributes stress much better than the traditional spline, increasing the shaft\220s max strength, torque, and lifespan. The gearbox housing was merged with the bushing mount and lid was changed to fit the modified output shaft.)/Pg 22 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

382 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 132 0 R/Pg 22 0 R/A[1389 0 R 0]/K[4]>>
endobj

383 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 132 0 R/E(Protective Safety Guards: Uses custom 3D printed guards to completely cover the rotation gears, claw linkages, both motors, and leadscrew to IP20 standards.Motor guards completely protect the motor and leadscrew. Gear guards completely protect the 2 gears used for rotation. Claw guards protect linkage pinch points from the top and bottom as well as sides. Each mount can easily be taken off for maintenance or replacement by removing only 2 bolts; all of them come off easily without having to remove any other components.)/Pg 22 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

384 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 132 0 R/E(Power Choice: For our manipulator we needed a way to move the connector piece for linear motion and a way to power the rotation. We decided to use brushless motors and a lead screw to achieve our needs. Using pneumatics for our linear motion would have been expensive, and requires pneumatic tubes to be run to the surface. Additionally no member of SMS has experience using pneumatics. unlike brushless motors, this is also one of the reasons for choosing brushless over servo or stepper motors for rotation of the claw. Waterproof servos were expensive and cheaper alternatives were too difficult to waterproof; stepper motors are also prone to corrode underwater. Therefore, two HobbyWater DD3130 brushless motors were purchased at a good price, providing a low kv for better torque, and are waterproof up to 300m. They are fast enough to turn our leadscrew quickly and offer 0.7Nm of torque which is enough grip onto objects and rotate the claw when using TPU grips and gearboxes.)/Pg 22 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

