434 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 137 0 R/E(At Sequoia Marine Solutions, safety is considered a core component of the engineering process. Safety is integrated into every stage of development, whether it\220s fabrication, testing, or operational procedures. The team prioritizes the protection of personnel, equipment, and the surrounding environment during the development of the ROV. Safety considerations are integrated into the design and development of the ROV to ensure it operates reliably while minimizing any electrical or mechanical hazards. With routine inspections, preventative maintenance, and proper PPE, Sequoia Marine Solutions is able to maintain a safety-focused engineering environment. )/Pg 27 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

435 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 137 0 R/E(Personnel Safety)/Pg 27 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

436 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 137 0 R/E(The safety rationale developed by Sequoia Marine Solutions is designed to protect all personnel involved in the creation of the ROV. All personnel working on the creation of the ROV are required to complete a lab safety training as well as a tool safety training to ensure proper handling of equipment. Sequoia Marine Solutions encourages all personnel to complete OSHA 10 training to strengthen overall workplace safety; however, the safety lead is expected to obtain certification in order to oversee that operations are meeting all safety standards. In addition, proper personal protective equipment \(PPE\) is needed whenever working on the ROV. The PPE consists of safety glasses, gloves, closed-toed shoes, and masks. Proper PPE is required when working with power tools or any equipment that can cause airborne fumes. When personnel are seen not to be using proper PPE, the Stop Work Authority Policy will kick in and halt all work until members who are in violation wear proper PPE. In addition, a warning will be issued to personnel, and repetitive offenses will lead to personnel not being able to work on ROV.)/Pg 27 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

437 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 137 0 R/E(Equipment Safety)/Pg 27 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

438 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 137 0 R/E(Sequoia Marine Solutions incorporates multiple safety features and inspection procedures to protect the ROV and any associated equipment. Electrical systems are protected through fuse protection, insulated wires, waterproof enclosures, and strain relief on tether and electrical components in the chassis. Thrust guards are )/Pg 27 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

439 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 137 0 R/E(installed to reduce accidental contact when propellers are in use during deployment and recovery of the ROV. In addition, bolts, fasteners, and structural components are inspected to ensure they\220re secure during the operation of the ROV in the water. Most importantly, a safety check-off list is conducted before and after all operations to ensure the overall safety of the ROV. This helps minimize equipment damage and improves reliability.)/Pg 27 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

440 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 137 0 R/E(Figure 35: CSO wearing proper PPE )/Pg 27 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

441 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 137 0 R/E(Operational Safety)/Pg 27 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

442 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 137 0 R/E(To ensure the safety of equipment and personnel a Jobsite Safety and Environment Analysis \(JSEA\) is conducted alongside a check off list to avoid any potential hazards to personnel, equipment, and environment. In addition, other safety measures like the Stop Work Authority are used as an additional safeguard for personnel and equipment. The Stop Work Authority is used whenever any Sequoia Marine Solutions personnel identifies an unsafe condition, hazardous action, or equipment failure. Operations will remain suspended until hazard has been implemented, and safety lead approves continuation of operation after corrective action has been completed. Sequoia Marine Solutions prioritizes safety, equipment protection, and mission success.)/Pg 27 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

