endobj

468 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 139 0 R/E(A week before qualifying, SMS swapped the backplate to a new anodized one with custom holes. SMS also added 3 new cameras, and filled the extra holes with Wetlink blanks, which introduced leakage problems. A compressed sponge was used to detect water leaks within the pressure hull when submerged. Before submersion, a test was done with a vacuum pump to see if the pressure hull would hold pressure, which was partially successful. After visual inspection the pressure hull was placed in the shallow end of the pool for a duration of 20 seconds. No water penetrated through to the sponges initially, so it was submerged for an additional two minutes in the shallow end. However, during the two minute test water entered the pressure hull.)/Pg 29 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

469 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 139 0 R/E(This leak location was identified by swelling in the sponge mesh, allowing for efficient correction. The culprit was a damaged o-ring on a Wetlink blank. The use of an incremental process expedited the identification of the root cause, exhibiting the successful application of water testing system to troubleshoot.)/Pg 29 0 R/K[14]>>
endobj

470 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 139 0 R/E(he thruster shrouds in comparison to an unshrouded thruster. In response, the thruster shrouds thickness was reduced and guarding holes were slightly opened, while still adhering to IP-20 standards.)/Pg 29 0 R/K[15]>>
endobj

